BooBoard patch for stable-diffusion.cpp master-1133-52491bd (see third_party/README.md).

ModelManager::ensure_host_capacity keeps 1 GB of free RAM spare before it
loads weights. That is a sensible margin on a desktop, but a phone has far
less memory to give: on a 4 GB device it leaves about 0.6 GB and loading the
1.7 GB LCM-Dreamshaper q8_0 model fails with "RAM weight capacity exceeded".
With the margin at 256 MB the same model loads and runs (about 1.5 GB free is
needed). Android's low-memory killer already protects the rest of the system,
and the model runs in a helper process, so only that process is at risk.

diff --git a/src/model_manager.cpp b/src/model_manager.cpp
--- a/src/model_manager.cpp
+++ b/src/model_manager.cpp
@@ -1309,7 +1309,8 @@
 }

